From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: Add ChimeraProtocOverride autoplugin: redirect protocExecutable to /usr/bin/protoc

sbt-protoc honors `PB.protocVersion` by downloading
`protoc-linux-x86_64-<ver>` from Maven into
$HOME/.cache/protocbridge.  That binary is glibc-linked and
fails to exec on musl with the usual ENOENT-shaped dynamic-
linker resolution failure.

Setting `ThisBuild / PB.protocExecutable := ...` in a `.sbt` file
at the build root doesn't take — sbt-protoc's `ProtocPlugin`
attaches a per-project default for `protocExecutable` derived
from `protocVersion`, and per-project scope beats ThisBuild.

The right fix is an AutoPlugin in `project/` that overrides
`protocExecutable` at projectSettings scope (same scope as the
plugin's own default) for every project that has ProtocPlugin
enabled.  `requires = ProtocPlugin` + `trigger = allRequirements`
makes it auto-apply.

cports' `protobuf` package provides /usr/bin/protoc (5.32.x);
proto3 syntax is fully forward-compatible at the wire and Java
codegen levels with the 3.17.3 sbt-protoc pin.

diff --git a/project/ChimeraProtocOverride.scala b/project/ChimeraProtocOverride.scala
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/project/ChimeraProtocOverride.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+import sbt._
+import sbt.Keys._
+import sbtprotoc.ProtocPlugin
+import sbtprotoc.ProtocPlugin.autoImport._
+
+/** Chimera-specific override.  The Adoptium / Maven-hosted protoc
+ *  pinned via PB.protocVersion is glibc-linked; cports' bldroot
+ *  is musl.  Redirect at /usr/bin/protoc (cports' protobuf pkg).
+ */
+object ChimeraProtocOverride extends AutoPlugin {
+  override def trigger = allRequirements
+  override def requires = ProtocPlugin
+  override lazy val projectSettings: Seq[Def.Setting[_]] = Seq(
+    PB.protocExecutable := file("/usr/bin/protoc")
+  )
+}
